  "description": "Construction of a part two storey part single storey rear extension and a two storey side extension including alterations to the existing front fenestration",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed development, by reason of its design, bulk, mass, scale and siting, would overly dominate the rear and side of the host dwelling, whilst also resulting in a detrimental loss of symmetry across the terrace row and the open aspect to the end-of-terrace dwelling. It would thereby cause harm to the character and appearance of the area, including&nbsp;moderate&nbsp;harm to the non-designated heritage asset. The proposal would therefore be contrary to the following policies which seek to ensure that developments are sympathetic to local character and historic distinctiveness:National Planning Policy Framework (NPPF) (December, 2024)Policy HC1 of the London Plan (March 2021) The Residential Extensions and Alterations Supplementary Planning Document (February 2012) Policies SPP6, SP2, DMD1, DMD4&nbsp;and DMD5 of The Barking and Dagenham Local Plan (September, 2024)"
  ],
